@meeting train.m5.brennan
// Pillar 5, M5 tuning, if Brennan teaches it (m5's by list is calder, brennan: only when Calder is off that day).
// The galley, Oven 1's panel. Head writer, seat W.
title: Tuning
from: Chef Auda Brennan
gist: Brennan showed you tuning: turn a setting a step at a time and watch the oven answer. Settle it and it's done.
== lines
brennan: Forty rolls, love. Burnt edges. This oven's got a temper.   [sigh]
brennan: Calder says nothing's broken. It's drifted. Like me after a double shift.
brennan > you: Watch the glow, not the dial. One click down. See? Calmer.   [gesture]
brennan: Another. There. Steady as a good stew. Done.
brennan: Too far and it sulks the other way. Just click it back.
? choice
* How do I know when it's right?   rel:brennan+2 flavour:practical
  brennan: When it stops stuttering and just glows. Same as a happy pan.   [nod]
* Why do ovens drift?   rel:brennan+1 flavour:listen
  brennan: Heat, use, and me slamming the door. Mostly me.   [laugh]
* Sorry about your rolls.   rel:brennan+1 flavour:cheer
  brennan: Not your fault, love. Settle the other one and we're square.
brennan: Oven 2's doing the same. Your turn. I'll be watching. Arms folded.
